<section>
<h1>Kasper College Library and Learning Resource Centre (LRC)</h1>
<p>Rules Governing Use, Learning Resources, Digital Subscriptions, and Student Facilities </P>

<div class = "textBox">
    <h2>1. Introduction & Purpose</h2>
    <p>The Kasper College Library and Learning Resource Centre (LRC) is a vibrant hub designed to support academic study, scholarly research, creative exploration, and collaborative project work. All registered students and current staff members of Kasper College are entitled to register as members of the LRC and utilize its extensive physical and digital resources for the duration of their course of study or employment.</p>
    <p>Membership and study access may also be extended to external researchers, alumni, and nominated individuals from partner organizations subject to registration approval and nominal administration fees. Use of LRC facilities implies full acceptance of the rules and regulations outlined below, which are designed to protect the rights, safety, and productivity of all users.</p>
</div>

<div class = "textBox">
    <h2>2. Access & Membership Rules</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><b>A. Institutional Access: <b>The use of the Library and Resource Centre facilities is strictly reserved for the educational, research, and scholarly purposes of Kasper College students and staff.</li>
        <li><b>B. Registration: <b>All individuals wishing to access the LRC must complete digital registration during enrollment and have their biometric or smart student/staff ID activated.</li>
        <li><b>C. External Visitors: <b>Individuals or organizations not eligible for automatic membership who have legitimate academic or research reasons to access the LRC may apply for a temporary Visitor Pass at the Reception Desk.</li>
        <li><b>D. Non-Transferability of ID Cards: <b>College ID cards are strictly personal and non-transferable. You must never lend your card to anyone else. Cardholders are responsible for all books, equipment, and resources borrowed on their account.</li>
        <li><b>E. Inspection of Identification: <b>LRC staff and campus security officers are authorized to request inspection of College ID cards at any time upon entering or while using LRC facilities.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class = "textBox">
    <h2>3. Facilities, Study Zones & Conduct Rules </h2>
    <ul>
        <li><b>A. Personal Belongings & Security: <b>The LRC accepts no responsibility for loss of, or damage to, personal belongings left unattended. Lockers are available in the lower concourse for daily use.</li>
        <li><b>B. Noise & Study Zones: <b>The LRC operates designated zoning:</li>
        <ul>
            <li><b>• Silent Research Floor (Level 3): </b>Strict individual silent study. No conversation or audio emissions permitted.</li>
            <li><b>• Quiet Study Floor (Level 2): </b>Whispered conversation permitted for academic queries only. Individual study carrels.</li>
            <li><b>• Collaborative Project Hub (Level 1): </b>Group discussion, team projects, and presentations permitted at reasonable volume.</li>
        </ul>
        <li><b>C. Mobile Phones & Personal Audio: <b>Mobile phones must be switched to silent mode across all study floors. Phone calls are strictly restricted to enclosed stairwell phone booths. Headphones must be used with audio at volumes that cannot be overheard by neighbors.</li>
        <li><b>D. Food & Beverage Policy: <b>Cold snacks and drinks in non-spill, securely lidded containers are permitted on Levels 1 and 2. Hot food, fast food, and open beverages are strictly prohibited across all LRC areas and near computer equipment.</li>
        <li><b>E. Electrical Safety & Mains Power: <b>Users may plug personal laptops, tablets, and phones into designated bench power outlets. Custom electrical appliances (e.g., heaters, kettles) or unapproved mains adapters are forbidden.</li>
        <li><b>F. Furniture & Equipment Care: <b>Defacing furniture, rearranging fixed workstations, or damaging books, hardware, and media is considered serious misconduct resulting in disciplinary review and repair cost recovery.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class = "textBox">
    <h2>4. Digital Subscriptions & Online Library Services </h2>
    <p>Kasper College maintains enterprise institutional subscriptions to premier digital libraries and databases accessible 24/7 on campus and remotely via Single Sign-On (SSO): </p>
    <ul>
        <li><b>ACM Digital Library: <b>Comprehensive collection of computing and information technology journals, conference proceedings, and technical magazines.</li>
        <li><b>IEEE Xplore Digital Library: <b>Premier access to IEEE journals, standards, and conference papers in electrical engineering, computer science, and networking.</li>
        <li><b>O'Reilly for Higher Education: <b>Over 50,000 tech ebooks, live courses, video tutorials, and interactive sandbox environments covering all modern programming languages, cloud platforms, and design tools.</li>
        <li><b>ScienceDirect & SpringerLink: <b> Extensive peer-reviewed scientific and technical literature spanning artificial intelligence, algorithms, human-computer interaction, and materials science.</li>
        <li><b>Statista & Mintel: <b>Global market data, consumer trends, and technology industry statistics for research and business case studies.</li>
        <li><b>Adobe Creative Cloud Campus License: <b>Full desktop access to Photoshop, Illustrator, Premiere Pro, After Effects, and XD across all LRC digital workstations.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class = "textBox">
    <h2>5. Equipment Loan Scheme </h2>
    <p>Registered students can borrow high-end technical equipment free of charge for coursework and project assignments from the LRC Loan Desk: </p>
    <ul>
        <li><b>High-Spec Laptops: <b>Dell XPS and MacBook Pro laptops loaded with developer environments (VS Code, Android Studio, Unity, Docker). 3-day and 7-day loan periods.</li>
        <li><b>Digital Cameras & Media Kits: <b>Sony 4K mirrorless cameras, directional shotgun microphones, LED light panels, and fluid-head tripods.</li>
        <li><b>Graphics Tablets & Styluses: <b>Wacom Intuos Pro and Cintiq companion tablets for digital illustration and 3D modeling.</li>
        <li><b>VR/AR Headsets: <b>Meta Quest 3 and HTC Vive developer kits for immersive game design and VR development.</li>
        <li><b>Microcontroller & IoT Kits: <b>Raspberry Pi 5 kits, Arduino Mega sets, ESP32 sensor bundles, and breadboards for embedded systems projects.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class = "textBox">
    <h2>6. Bookable Study Spaces & Printing Services </h2>
    <ul>
        <li><b>Group Study Rooms (Rooms 101 – 108): <b>Equipped with 75-inch 4K collaborative displays, wireless Apple AirPlay / Miracast connectivity, and glass dry-erase whiteboards. Bookable up to 7 days in advance via the student portal (max 3 hours per booking).</li>
        <li><b>Podcast & Media Recording Studio: <b>A soundproof acoustic studio with Shure SM7B broadcast microphones, audio interface, and multi-track recording software.</li>
        <li><b>Follow-Me Printing & Scanning: <b>High-speed multi-function printers on all floors supporting cloud printing, duplex A4/A3 color printing, high-res scanning to email, and wide-format poster printing.</li>
        <li><b>3D Printing & Binding Station: <b>PLA and resin 3D printers available for rapid prototyping, alongside comb, wire, and thermal binding machines for dissertation submissions.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class = "textBox">
    <h2>7. Academic Skills & Subject Librarian Consultations </h2>
    <ul>
        <li><b>Subject Librarians: <b>Dedicated computing and design librarians available for 1-to-1 appointments to assist with literature reviews, database querying, and referencing (Harvard, IEEE, APA).</li>
        <li><b>Academic Writing Workshops: <b>Weekly drop-in sessions covering technical report writing, dissertation structuring, and ethical academic conduct.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class = "textBox">
    <h2>8. LRC Opening Hours & Contact </h2>
    <ul>
        <li><b>Term-Time Operating Hours: <b>Building open 24/7 with active ID swipe card. Staffed Helpdesk & Loan Counter: Monday – Friday 08:00 – 20:00 | Saturday – Sunday 10:00 – 17:00.</li>
        <li><b>Vacation Operating Hours: <b>Monday – Friday 08:30 – 17:30 (Closed Bank Holidays).</li>
        <li><b>Helpdesk Telephone: <b>(01321) 2340 238</li>
        <li><b>Library Email: <b>library@kaspercollege.ac.uk</li>
        <li><b>Digital Catalogue URL: <b>https://library.kaspercollege.ac.uk</li>
    </ul>
</div>
</section>